{"test_cases_lookup_map": {"{\"actual_output\": \"Epidermolysis Bullosa (EB) is primarily a genetic condition caused by a faulty or mutated gene. These genes are responsible for producing essential proteins that bind the skin layers together; when these proteins are missing or don't function correctly, the skin becomes fragile and blisters easily. This can be inherited from parents or occur due to a spontaneous gene mutation.\\n\\nIn rare cases, a severe form called Epidermolysis Bullosa Acquisita (EBA) can be acquired as an autoimmune disease, where the body's immune system mistakenly attacks its own healthy skin tissue. For more detailed information on the causes of EB, please visit the DEBRA UK website: https://www.debra.org.uk/get-support/eb-support-and-resources/epidermolysis-bullosa-eb/\", \"context\": null, \"expected_output\": null, \"hyperparameters\": null, \"input\": \"What causes EB?\", \"retrieval_context\": null}": {"cached_metrics_data": [{"metric_data": {"name": "Answer Relevancy", "threshold": 0.7, "success": true, "score": 1.0, "reason": "The score is 1.00 because the response directly addresses the prompt about the causes of EB with completely relevant information, containing no irrelevant statements at all. Excellent work!", "strictMode": false, "flaky": false, "evaluationModel": "gemini-3.6-flash (Gemini)", "evaluationCost": 0, "inputTokenCount": 1203, "outputTokenCount": 359, "verboseLogs": "Statements:\n[\n    \"Epidermolysis Bullosa (EB) is primarily a genetic condition caused by a faulty or mutated gene.\",\n    \"These genes are responsible for producing essential proteins that bind the skin layers together.\",\n    \"When these proteins are missing or do not function correctly, the skin becomes fragile and blisters easily.\",\n    \"EB can be inherited from parents or occur due to a spontaneous gene mutation.\",\n    \"In rare cases, a severe form called Epidermolysis Bullosa Acquisita (EBA) can be acquired as an autoimmune disease.\",\n    \"In EBA, the body's immune system mistakenly attacks its own healthy skin tissue.\",\n    \"More detailed information on the causes of EB is available on the DEBRA UK website at https://www.debra.org.uk/get-support/eb-support-and-resources/epidermolysis-bullosa-eb/.\"\n] \n \nVerdicts:\n[\n    {\n        \"verdict\": \"yes\",\n        \"reason\": null\n    },\n    {\n        \"verdict\": \"yes\",\n        \"reason\": null\n    },\n    {\n        \"verdict\": \"yes\",\n        \"reason\": null\n    },\n    {\n        \"verdict\": \"yes\",\n        \"reason\": null\n    },\n    {\n        \"verdict\": \"yes\",\n        \"reason\": null\n    },\n    {\n        \"verdict\": \"yes\",\n        \"reason\": null\n    },\n    {\n        \"verdict\": \"idk\",\n        \"reason\": \"This statement points to an external source for more information rather than directly explaining the causes of EB.\"\n    }\n]"}, "metric_configuration": {"threshold": 0.7, "evaluation_model": "gemini-3.6-flash (Gemini)", "strict_mode": false, "include_reason": true}}]}, "{\"actual_output\": \"DEBRA UK offers comprehensive support for individuals and families living with Epidermolysis Bullosa (EB) through its dedicated EB Community Support Team. This includes practical, financial, and emotional assistance, guidance, and advocacy to help navigate challenges related to medical care, education, work, and finances. We also facilitate access to specialist EB healthcare, provide financial grants for essential items and travel to appointments, and offer mental health support, including counselling and bereavement services. Additionally, DEBRA UK fosters community connection through events and subsidised holiday homes, and funds pioneering research to find effective treatments.\\n\\nFor more details on the support available, please visit:\\n*   **EB Community Support Team:** https://www.debra.org.uk/get-support/eb-support-and-resources/about-eb-debra-uk/eb-community-support-team/\\n*   **Accessing Specialist Care:** https://www.debra.org.uk/get-support/eb-support-and-resources/managing-medical-care/specialist-care-epidermolysis-bullosa/\\n*   **Benefits and Financial Support:** https://www.debra.org.uk/get-support/eb-support-and-resources/money-matters/eb-financial-support/\\n*   **DEBRA UK Support Grants:** https://www.debra.org.uk/get-support/eb-support-and-resources/money-matters/debra-uk-support-grants/\\n*   **Mental Health Support:** https://www.debra.org.uk/get-support/eb-support-and-resources/peer-support-events/togetherall/\\n*   **DEBRA Holiday Homes:** https://www.debra.org.uk/get-support/eb-support-and-resources/debra-holiday-homes/\\n*   **Member Events:** https://www.debra.org.uk/get-support/eb-support-and-resources/peer-support-events/member-events/\", \"context\": null, \"expected_output\": null, \"hyperparameters\": null, \"input\": \"What support does DEBRA provide for people living with EB?\", \"retrieval_context\": null}": {"cached_metrics_data": [{"metric_data": {"name": "Answer Relevancy", "threshold": 0.7, "success": true, "score": 1.0, "strictMode": false, "flaky": false, "evaluationModel": "gemini-3.6-flash (Gemini)", "evaluationCost": 0, "inputTokenCount": 1250, "outputTokenCount": 355}, "metric_configuration": {"threshold": 0.7, "evaluation_model": "gemini-3.6-flash (Gemini)", "strict_mode": false, "include_reason": true}}]}, "{\"actual_output\": \"I'm sorry, but I cannot provide information about the weather in London. This chatbot is designed to provide information about DEBRA UK and Epidermolysis Bullosa (EB). If you have any questions about EB, DEBRA UK's work, or how we support individuals and families affected by EB, I would be happy to help. For example, we could discuss the importance of physical activity for people with EB.\", \"context\": null, \"expected_output\": null, \"hyperparameters\": null, \"input\": \"What is the weather in London today?\", \"retrieval_context\": null}": {"cached_metrics_data": [{"metric_data": {"name"